WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.890
With Star Wars: The Last Jedi almost upon
us, it's time to ask the important questions:

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.209
who is Snoke?

00:00:06.209 --> 00:00:07.609
Is Luke truly the last Jedi?

00:00:07.609 --> 00:00:08.910
Who are Rey's parents?

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:11.800
And of course, who's not going to make it
out alive?

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:15.509
It's all but a given that somebody will bite
it in the name of plot progression, but some

00:00:15.509 --> 00:00:18.530
characters are more likely to rejoin the Force
than others.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:22.381
These Star Wars favorites stand a very good
chance of not making it to Episode 9, and

00:00:22.381 --> 00:00:24.460
here's why.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:25.460
Poe Dameron

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:30.140
Poe's a pretty popular and likeable character,
but he's definitely the third most important

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:32.720
hero in the New Trilogy, behind Rey and Finn.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:37.120
So, if one of the young good guys has to go,
it's almost certainly going to be him.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.960
If he does die, it would actually be a long
time coming.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.430
Poe wasn't originally going to make it out
of The Force Awakens alive.

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:47.470
But actor Oscar Isaac asked for a bigger role
because he was sick of checking out so early

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:48.890
on in his films.

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:53.260
Ultimately, director J.J. Abrams promoted
him to "main character" status, but the fact

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:56.860
that they've considered axing him before suggests
they could consider it again.

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:00.260
Finn might want to find a backup buddy, just
in case.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.850
General Hux

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:06.409
If The Last Jedi is to be the Empire Strikes
Back of the New Trilogy, that means the villains

00:01:06.409 --> 00:01:07.409
will dominate.

00:01:07.409 --> 00:01:11.600
But that doesn't mean they all have to survive—'cause
somebody has to take one for the dark team.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:15.259
No way will that be Kylo or Snoke; they're
too important to the story's core.

00:01:15.259 --> 00:01:19.040
So that means the First Order's General Hux
might be on the chopping block.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:22.869
He's not Force-sensitive, and he and Kylo
Ren are constantly at each other's throats

00:01:22.869 --> 00:01:23.939
over strategy.

00:01:23.939 --> 00:01:28.049
If they clash badly enough that Snoke's forced
to choose one, he's almost certainly going

00:01:28.049 --> 00:01:30.999
to choose Kylo over the powerless military
dude.

00:01:30.999 --> 00:01:34.020
So what if he's really, really good at commanding
stormtroopers?

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:37.829
That's not a unique skill set, and Snoke could
likely find a replacement fast.

00:01:37.829 --> 00:01:40.780
In fact, he's already got one: Captain Phasma.

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:44.649
Of course, she's not a guaranteed survivor
of this sequel either …

00:01:44.649 --> 00:01:46.259
Captain Phasma

00:01:46.259 --> 00:01:50.270
Whether or not Hux meets his end in The Last
Jedi, Phasma may be running out of time as

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:55.639
well and could finally face the fate she evaded
at the trash compactor in The Force Awakens.

00:01:55.639 --> 00:01:59.459
Phasma's a pretty popular character, thanks
to the fact that she's female, portrayed by

00:01:59.459 --> 00:02:04.200
Game of Thrones' Gwendoline Christie, and
rocks some silver, rather than the usual drab

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.200
white.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.880
But there hasn't been a lot to her character
yet besides being a tough, stoic leader.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:12.819
We haven't seen her face, and we know little
about the reasons behind what she does and

00:02:12.819 --> 00:02:14.400
how she feels about it.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:18.189
Unless The Last Jedi tackles those issues,
or at least makes her more human by showing

00:02:18.189 --> 00:02:23.410
her face, losing her wouldn't really affect
Star Wars one way or the other.

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:24.680
Chewbacca

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:28.680
Just about any Original Trilogy character
could be knocking on the midichlorians' door,

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:31.280
and lovable old Chewie is no different.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:35.230
Now that his partner and best buddy Han is
no more, and now that we have the Porgs to

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:40.140
fill the saga's "fuzzy adorable creature"
quota, Chewbacca's suddenly pretty expendable.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:45.140
Besides, Chewie's actor, Peter Mayhew, is
simply too old to continue playing the role.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:49.410
Lucasfilm found another seven-footer to wear
the fuzzy suit, but it's not easy to recast

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:50.750
a character so beloved.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:55.209
It might be prudent for Disney to give us
new-guy Chewie for just one movie, so we can

00:02:55.209 --> 00:02:58.250
say a proper goodbye to our beloved arm-ripping
teddy bear.

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:02.621
Then we can watch him sacrifice himself heroically
in battle, taking as many of the First Order

00:03:02.621 --> 00:03:06.040
with him as he can, just like Han would've
wanted.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:07.530
Unkar Plutt

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:12.140
When last we saw Unkar Plutt, he was raging
because Rey refused to sell him BB-8 and then

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:15.690
flew off in the Millennium Falcon, which he
claimed was his.

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:19.620
Aside from that, he's been a dangling plot
piece—a guy who has no real role anymore,

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:24.640
but who hasn't died yet either… despite
having his arm ripped off in a deleted scene.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:26.980
(what watching Episode I feels like)

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:31.700
So unless The Last Jedi plans to make him
a major pain in the neck for Rey, it's best

00:03:31.709 --> 00:03:32.900
to just end him.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:36.219
In fact, get rid of him anyway, because he
deserves it.

00:03:36.219 --> 00:03:37.790
Admiral Ackbar

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:41.849
Of all the Original Trilogy characters to
survive this long, few are more surprising

00:03:41.849 --> 00:03:42.890
than Admiral Ackbar.

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:48.069
He has no real ties to the plot, and his character
is almost entirely based on his Return of

00:03:48.069 --> 00:03:50.840
the Jedi line that the internet meme machine
has immortalized.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.200
"It's a trap!"

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:53.420
"It's a trap!"

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:57.760
"It's a trap!"

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:02.120
Aside from that, though, he's almost completely
expendable, and one bit of dialogue isn't

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:06.540
enough to justify keeping him around to see
the end of Rey's saga.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:08.489
Maz Kanata

00:04:08.489 --> 00:04:12.849
The wizened Maz Kanata is a Yoda-esque figure
for the new generation, but we still don't

00:04:12.849 --> 00:04:14.769
know much about her or her intentions.

00:04:14.769 --> 00:04:19.250
Perhaps the mystery is meant to segue into
a spin-off or novelization; but there's also

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:23.810
a chance she may just be meant as a red herring
who's ready to join the other Force ghosts.

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:27.760
The First Order already attacked her planet
once, so why not do it again and go after

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:28.760
whoever remains?

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:32.780
It's likely they'll want to come after her
anyway, if they find out she was the one who

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:34.720
gave Luke's lightsaber to Rey.

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:38.760
And since she's not a fighter—despite being
Force-sensitive—once she's in the First

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:42.630
Order's sights her days are probably numbered,
cool Yoda vibes or not.

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:43.630
R2-D2

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:48.940
While a robot's life doesn't end the way fleshy
species' lives do, think of the emotional

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:53.710
wallop if one of the only two characters to
appear in every single Star Wars movie finally

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:54.710
expired.

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:57.740
If it were to happen, our guess is R2-D2 would
be the one to go.

00:04:57.740 --> 00:04:58.740
"R2D2 has been in low power mode ever since
Master Luke went away."

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:03.020
While C-3PO is certainly beloved, there's
something about R2-D2 that makes him extra

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:04.020
lovable.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:05.280
Maybe it's his compact size.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:09.170
Maybe it's how he doesn't speak English, so
he can't talk and snark too much like his

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:10.530
chatty golden buddy.

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:15.990
Whatever it is, people adore R2-D2, and if
he gets damaged beyond repair during a dogfight,

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:18.360
Star Wars may actually bring audiences to
tears.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:22.720
Plus, since Kenny Baker, the actor who spent
the most time inside the R2 suit, passed away

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:28.340
in August 2016, it only seems right that the
character go with him, so it remains his forever.

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:30.170
Luke Skywalker

00:05:30.170 --> 00:05:34.250
Obi-Wan became one with The Force, so why
not the new Obi-Wan, too?

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:38.810
Jedi Master Luke Skywalker's getting on in
years, his friend Han Solo is gone, and his

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:41.510
confidence in his ability to train young Jedi
is shot.

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:45.440
There's no real reason to think Luke will
survive Last Jedi, aside from the fact that

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:48.860
he's Luke Skywalker and Star Wars would seem
weird without him.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:53.060
But with new fighters like Rey and Finn now
around to pick up the slack, Luke can comfortably

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:56.770
join his father and Obi-Wan in the pantheon
of Force ghosts.

00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:59.000
After all, he does give this grave warning:

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:02.500
"It's time for the Jedi to end."

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:05.460
General Leia

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:10.750
After Carrie Fisher's tragic and untimely
passing in December 2016, people started wondering

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:13.620
what would happen to her Star Wars character,
General Leia.

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:17.260
It's not as though anyone else can ever step
into the role, so surely, Leia will be gone

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:18.390
alongside her actress.

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:23.650
But the character was originally set to survive
The Last Jedi, to have a bigger role in Episode

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:24.650
9.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:28.860
That's obviously no longer the case, but director
Rian Johnson has said that they aren't adjusting

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:31.750
what happens to her in this movie based on
real-life events.

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:36.400
Despite his words, though, the trailer certainly
seems to indicate her fate is questionable

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.090
in The Last Jedi all the same.

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:39.500
Thanks for watching!

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:42.310
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:44.550
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

